      "statement": "Necho's objective in 609 was Carchemish on the Euphrates (2 Chr 35:20; 1 Esd 1:25).",
      "layer": "reconstruction",
      "passage": "2Chr.35.20",
      "classification": "disputed",
      "reasoning": "Chronicles and 1 Esdras name Carchemish; Kings names the king of Assyria and the Euphrates; ABC 3 shows the 609 Egyptian army crossing the Euphrates against Harran, without naming the crossing point. Keil takes Carchemish at face value; Curtis and Madsen hold that the writer introduced it from Necho's defeat there in 605. Carchemish as a crossing point on the way to Harran would reconcile the sources but is not attested for 609 in the texts read.",
